  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 231 PM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nMinimally impactful weather is forecast through this weekend. For the \nrest of today and tonight an upper-level low will move across \nsouthern WI bring and increase in cloud cover to the region. An arc \nof light showers has developed along the WI/MN border and will \nslowly drift east through the evening, however, with dry mid-level \nair in place, don't expect more than a sprinkle to reach central WI \nfor before the precip dries away. While cloud cover tonight will \nkeep temperatures from bottoming out the presence of a cooler air \nmass will allow lows to reach the low to middle 30s across north-\ncentral WI which may result in patchy areas of frost in protected \nand low laying areas. A similar set up is expected Tuesday night, \nhowever, lows be a few degrees warmer as winds become more easterly. \n\nWith a Hudson Bay high expected to remain entrenched through next \nweekend any weak short-waves moving towards the region will struggle \nto produce any measurable rainfall. The next chance for more \nwidespread rain does not look to come until this high starts to \nbreak down and a long wave trough moves passes across the region \nearly next week.\n\nTemperatures this week will gradually trend warmer each day with \nhighs climbing back into the upper 60s to low 70s by the weekend.",
